# Data stores

PostgreSQL (source of truth, relational data):
- Every schema change is a migration. Never edit an applied migration.
- snake_case tables/columns, `id uuid`, `created_at`/`updated_at timestamptz`.
- Unique constraints enforce invariants (e.g. `(source, external_id)` on jobs).
- Parameterized queries only; never interpolate strings into SQL.

MongoDB (raw / flexible / append-heavy data):
- Raw source payloads and AI generation history only. No data the app must join on.
- Every collection has an explicit index list and, where useful, a TTL index.

Both:
- Repositories return domain types, not driver objects.
- Changes to tables/collections must update the `erDiagram` in the feature doc.
